# The CSV fixtures are byte fixtures. Their line endings are part of what they
# test, not an artifact of whoever last saved them.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true stores them LF-normalized, so the CRLF that
# prisma/fixtures/README.md documents as a deliberate hazard survives only in a
# Windows working copy. A fresh clone on Linux — CI, or a Vercel build — gets
# LF, and the parser is then verified against a file shaped differently from the
# one the README describes.
#
# `-text` means no conversion in either direction: the bytes committed are the
# bytes checked out, everywhere.
prisma/fixtures/*.csv -text
fixtures/sample-headers.csv -text
